# Layer separation

- `src/handlers/` — Telegram I/O only: parse updates, call services, format replies. No SQL, no repository imports.
- `src/services/` — business logic and orchestration. Depends on database abstractions, not on Telegram types.
- `src/database/` — persistence only (queries, models, migrations). No Telegram, no domain policy.

```python
# BAD — handler talks to DB
async def on_status(message: Message) -> None:
    row = await db.fetch_user(message.from_user.id)

# GOOD — handler → service
async def on_status(message: Message) -> None:
    status = await user_service.get_status(message.from_user.id)
    await message.answer(format_status(status))
```
